<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb industrial output down revised 3.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb industrial output down revised 3.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in February fell a revised 3.7 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 3.4 percent fall, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year comparison, industrial production in February rose a revised 3.1 percent, against a preliminary estimate of a 3.4 percent increase.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  FEB     PRELIM    MONTH AGO FEBINDEX</p>
<p> Output		 -3.7    -3.4    +5.6    101.9</p>
<p> Shipments	    -4.3    -4.0    +6.4    104.1</p>
<p> Inventories	  -0.7    -0.7     0.0    106.3</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   +0.8    +0.5    -3.5    108.7</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>			  FEB     PRELIM    MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output		 +3.1    +3.4    +8.9</p>
<p> Shipments	    +4.0    +4.3   +10.8</p>
<p> Inventories	  -3.3    -3.4    -2.5</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   -4.9    -5.2    -9.0</p>
</text>
